  "summary": "Design, assessment and open access are being combined within single tools for hybrid capture probes, oligo DNA libraries and CRISPR knockout feasibility.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is computational design and assessment of molecular reagents, delivered as open software. BaitBench is a Rust tool that unifies hybrid capture probe design, assessment and thermodynamic simulation, with CLI and GUI access, and reports a correlation of rho=0.916 in its assessment. PoolParty builds oligo pool DNA libraries as computational graphs, with more than 50 mutagenesis, motif and barcode operations. tWhEEL pairs transcript-aware gene redundancy inference with CRISPR guide designs to score knockout feasibility. Other items apply computational methods to adjacent problems, including LLM-agent interrogation of LC-MS/MS and transcriptomic data, MCP-based gene-level evidence synthesis, and literature-mined purification parameters, and do not share the design focus. The new element is the combination of design, assessment and open access within single tools rather than separate design and evaluation stages.",
